extend-clock-sleep-to-sixteen-hours

Lane: backend

FlatPatch: extend-clock-sleep-to-sixteen-hours

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Allow clock.sleep to wait for up to sixteen hours in one call.

Requires: none

Provides: Set the shared tool declaration and duration validation maximum to 57600000 milliseconds, preserving the one-millisecond minimum and native interruptible sleep execution.

Boundary: Clock registration, time providers, input interruption, turn cancellation, clock failure policy, item notifications and analytics remain native owners.

Verification: Controlled current_time_reminder tests verify the advertised maximum, full-duration provider dispatch and rejection above the limit; App Server sleep tests verify maximum-duration interruption, analytics and external-clock failure handling without a real sixteen-hour wait.


